      "writtenOn": "2023-12-12T11:33:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gwendal, \n\nThanks for clarify and explanation.\n\nBut I have one more questions need discuss with you, from my searching in EC code, the `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_MAX_SENSOR_FREQ_MILLIHZ` is 125000 on dedede and octopus baord, but on Nissa, it is set to 100000. \n\nWhat guidelines are baseboard setting this value according to?",
      "parentUuid": "8f926466_7ed40259",
      "revId": "db6993cffbcb9ab0eed0e0f6ed13864c662a9cd7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "48955492_15d7e7a7",
        "filename": "include/driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso_public.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-12T16:26:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The value is set to the maximum sensor frequency the EC can handle. By default it is 250Hz. Some EC can handle up to 400Hz, but some EC are not powerful enough and the value should be reduced. 125Hz is a good choice since it allows sensors to run at 104Hz.",
      "parentUuid": "83d0935c_8f06323f",
      "revId": "db6993cffbcb9ab0eed0e0f6ed13864c662a9cd7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
